gram (Weekdays, Sat. and Sun.) OFF 1, 3, 6, 12 months or OFF to disable OFF 1 to 12 months or OFF to disable 0 : Flow through type humidifier (1 reminder per season) 1 : Drain-less type humidifier (2 reminders per season) OFF 1 to 12 months or OFF to disable OFF 1 to 12 months or OFF to disable 0 = WAKE and SLEEP 1 = WAKE, LEAVE, RETURN, SLEEP ** If humidifier type is set to Drain-less, then the first reminder is based on the system setting 21, second reminder will activate 3 months later. If humidifier type is set to Flow through, then the first reminder is based on system setting 21, second reminder will activate 12 months later. 15","SYSTEM TEST MODE The system test mode is used to test a system after installation. The outputs of the thermostat can be manually activated one at a time to test their function. The following instructions show how to enter the test mode and turn outputs on and off. The charts on the following pages show all of the options for each model. The test steps are: Test Number 50 51 52 53 Heat/Cool Models 8444, 8463, 8448HC, 8466HC Heating (W) (W2) Cooling (Y) (Y2) Fan (G) Heat Pump Models 8446, 8465, 8448HP, 8466HP Aux Heating (W) (W2) Compressor Cooling (Y) (Y2) Compressor Heating (Y) (Y2) Fan (G) HOW TO ENTER THE SYSTEM TEST MENU Press repeatedly until system is set to OFF. Press and hold seconds. and for three The screen of the first test step #50 is displayed: SYSTEM TEST NUMBER OUTPUT STATUS FLASHES IF 24VAC IS NOT PRESENT MODE (SW1 SETTING 8448 & 8466 ONLY) Press to turn on the output (01). For multi stage output, press again to turn on the 2nd stage (02). Press to turn off the output (00). Press to change to the next test step. Press after the last test step. DONE will be displayed. The thermostat will return to Normal mode if no key is pressed in 20 seconds. 16 17","TEST STEPS FOR 8444 & 8463 Step Key Input System Setting #2 #50 Heat #51 Cool #52 Fan [UP] [DOWN] [UP] [DOWN] [UP] [DOWN] 0 : Gas 1 : Elec 01 HEATING ON (W) ON ON Display